{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.le_trM_of_le_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.le_trM_of_le_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L204-L210","doc":"The mirror lower bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_le_of_normalised_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_le_of_normalised_le","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L193-L202","doc":"**Convexity bound.** Under a probability block measure the Markov trace is a\nconvex combination of the normalised characters, hence bounded by any common\nupper bound of them. This fails for a weight family that does not sum to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.blockMass_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.blockMass_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L190-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.IsProbability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.IsProbability","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L184-L188","doc":"Non-negative weights: the block masses form a probability vector\n(non-negative, summing to `1` by `blockMass_sum_eq_one`). Carried as a\nhypothesis; the corpus measures it for convention D and does not yet prove it at\ngeneral `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level_le_level_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level_le_level_one","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L170-L174","doc":"Consequently the unit's level dominates every other element's level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level_one_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level_one_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L163-L168","doc":"**The unit sits at the top level.** For any energy ranking of the blocks, the\ntrivial closure has the maximal level — so an energy-ranked level cannot place the\nidentity (or a free constituent product's neutral element) at level `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.charSupp_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.charSupp_one","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L157-L161","doc":"At the unit, the character support is everything: `χ_λ(1) = dim V_λ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_eq_expectation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_eq_expectation","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L148-L155","doc":"**The trace is an expectation.** With every block of nonzero dimension, the\nMarkov trace is the `blockMass`-weighted sum of the normalised characters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level_le_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level_le_top","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L137-L139","doc":"Every level is at most the top rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.level","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L131-L135","doc":"The energy-ranked level of `x` for an energy ranking `E : Λ → ℕ` of the\nblocks: the rank of the most expensive block in the (character) support. This\nis the shape of `def:confinement-level`, `ℓ(K, q) = min{ℓ : T_w ∈ J^ℓ(q)}` with\n`J^ℓ` spanned by the blocks of rank `≤ ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.charSupp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.charSupp","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L126-L129","doc":"Character support of `x`: the blocks on which its character is nonzero.\nA lower bound for the block support (a nonzero traceless block is invisible). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_eq_of_entangledSupp_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_eq_of_entangledSupp_empty","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L112-L124","doc":"If no block separates `a` from `b`, their Markov traces agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.entangledSupp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.entangledSupp","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L107-L110","doc":"Blocks on which two elements have different characters — the block set a\nbound word `a` and its free constituent product `b` do **not** share. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.blockMass_sum_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.blockMass_sum_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L100-L105","doc":"**Normalisation.** The block masses sum to `1` — Markov axiom M1 read\nthrough the Frobenius pairing at `x = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.blockMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.blockMass","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L97-L98","doc":"The mass the pairing assigns to a block: `y_λ · dim V_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM_one","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Markov axiom M1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.χ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.χ_one","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L86-L86","doc":"A character at the unit is the dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.pairing","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The Frobenius pairing `tr_M = Σ_λ y_λ χ_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.dim","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The dimension of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.χ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.χ","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The character of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.y","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The Markov (Frobenius-pairing) weight of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.trM","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData","kind":"structure","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing.lean#L69-L88","doc":"Abstract Frobenius-pairing data for a Markov trace on a finite block set `Λ`:\n`trM x = ∑ λ, y λ * χ λ x`, with `χ λ 1 = dim λ` and the Markov axiom M1\n`trM 1 = 1`. The characters are carried as functions `A → R`; nothing about\ntheir linearity or class-function property is needed below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}